Original commit body from 967756a:

"Hot spots" in standard dev tooling means high-risk areas needing more
tests. Our usage (high test density) was the opposite - well-tested code.

Rename to "test_dense" which accurately describes what it shows: functions
with high tests-per-LOC ratio, which may indicate redundant tests or
over-tested utilities.

This naming makes more sense in the agentic development context where
100% coverage is table-stakes and tracking test concentration helps
identify potential redundancy.
